A: What exactly is data labeling?

Data labeling is the process of assigning meaningful labels, categories or annotations to raw data so that machine-learning systems can learn from or be evaluated against that data.


"How do you ensure accuracy when labeling data?"

"I start by understanding the labeling guidelines and definitions before beginning the task. I evaluate each item against those guidelines consistently rather than relying on intuition alone.

I also perform a second review when an example is borderline or contains multiple conditions. If something is ambiguous, I check the documentation and use the project's escalation process rather than guessing.

I would also pay attention to recurring mistakes so I can prevent them in future tasks. For me, consistency is just as important as speed because inconsistent labels can reduce the quality of the dataset."

Q: "How would you evaluate an AI-generated answer?"

A: I would first identify what the user's prompt requires and then evaluate the response against those requirements. I would check instruction following, factual accuracy, relevance, completeness, clarity, internal consistency and safety. I would separate personal preference from objective quality and apply whatever rubric or guidelines the project provides.


